description: How to spend one day in Niwot, Colorado — coffee on Second Avenue, the historic block, the public art, lunch on a patio, the trail out to the fields and dinner before the drive home, with everything within a short walk.
navKey: things-to-do
permalink: /one-day-in-niwot/
ogImage: second-avenue-patios.jpg
ogImageAlt: Patios and hanging baskets on the 300 block of Second Avenue in Niwot
pageStyles: |
  .n-stop{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(86px,.14fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(14px,2.5vw,40px);align-items:start;padding:26px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule)}
  .n-stop:first-child{border-top:3px solid var(--n-red)}
  .n-clock{font-family:var(--n-serif);font-size:clamp(1.125rem,1rem + .5vw,1.5rem);line-height:1.15;color:var(--n-red-ink)}
  .n-two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(24px,3vw,56px);align-items:start}
  .n-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(16px,2vw,32px)}
  @media (max-width:760px){.n-stop{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:6px}}
  @media (max-width:900px){.n-two{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
  @media (max-width:620px){.n-pair{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}
# The shape of the day. The times are a suggested order of things, not
# opening hours — this site does not publish those anywhere, and each stop
# links to the business or the county page that does.
stops:
  - clock: Morning
    title: Coffee on Second Avenue
    body: Start on the 100 and 200 blocks with a coffee and something baked. The Old Oak Coffeehouse is at 136 Second Avenue, and Emory Jane’s mobile espresso bar is out around Niwot on some days — where it parks changes, and the operator publishes the schedule. Sit outside if the tables are out — the morning is the quiet part of the day here.
    links:
      - label: Coffee, bakery and sweets
        href: /restaurants/#coffee-sweets
  - clock: Late morning
    title: Walk the historic block
    body: Second Avenue end to end takes about ten minutes if you do not stop, and considerably longer if you do. The brick and false-front buildings date from the railroad period and the street grid runs at an angle to everything around it, which is the 1875 plat still showing. The shops, the antiques and the galleries are all on this walk.
    links:
      - label: The Old Town guide
        href: /old-town-niwot/
      - label: Why the street runs at an angle
        href: /history/
  - clock: Midday
    title: The caboose, and the public art
    body: Whistle Stop Park is at the western end of the block, at Murray Street and First Avenue, with CB&Q 14649 — a Burlington Route caboose built in 1907 — standing on a short length of track. The steel gateway sculpture is at the highway edge of the community, and further works are sited around the commercial blocks.
    links:
      - label: Parks and trails
        href: /parks-trails/
      - label: Public art
        href: /things-to-do/#art
  - clock: Lunch
    title: A patio, if the weather allows
    body: Cottonwood Square is a fifteen-minute walk north-east and holds the second cluster of kitchens, with two bronze bears on the corner. Several places across the two blocks describe outdoor seating on their own pages, and the restaurant guide lists which; the rest may have tables out without saying so.
    links:
      - label: Where to eat
        href: /restaurants/
  - clock: Afternoon
    title: Out to the fields
    body: East of the blocks the sidewalks stop and the farmland starts. The LoBo Regional Trail runs through Niwot between Longmont and Boulder — twelve miles end to end — and the local paths connect to it. Check the county's closures page before setting out, and take its Niwot trails map with you.
    links:
      - label: The trails, and the county's rules
        href: /parks-trails/
  - clock: Evening
    title: Dinner, and whatever is on
    body: Niwot has Italian on two blocks, Mexican and Chinese on the square, sushi at the back of the market, a brewery and a bar with its own kitchen. On a summer Thursday there is a free concert on the park lawn; on a second Friday the shops stay open late for the art walk; on the Friday evenings of the season there is dancing on the square.
    links:
      - label: What is on
        href: /events/
      - label: Rock & Rails
        href: /events/rock-and-rails/
---
